programs. In fact, the priority that the university places on diversity and inclusion, as well as the very frequent, active conversations surrounding how to \"do better\" were major factors in Jacqueline's decision to start the lab at UC Santa Cruz."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"statement","children":"We do not tolerate racism, sexism, homophobia or bigotry. Period."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"resource-list","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"https://stemdiv.ucsc.edu/","children":"stemdiv.ucsc.edu"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://diversity.ucsc.edu/","children":"diversity.ucsc.edu"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://pbse.ucsc.edu/about/pbse-clubs-groups.html","children":"PBSE clubs and groups"}]]}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"poster-frame","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/kimmeylab/images/diversity-poster.jpeg","alt":"In this lab, we believe: science is real, love is love, Black lives matter, feminism is for everyone, bacteria are cool, immigrants are welcome."}]}]]}],["$","footer",null,{"className":"footer","id":"contact","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/kimmeylab/logo/ucsc logo.png","alt":"UC Santa Cruz"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Kimmey Lab"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Department of Microbiology and Environmental Toxicology"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Biomedical Sciences, UC Santa Cruz"}]]}]]}]]}]
